  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "statement": "You are given a sequence of N integers arriving one at a time. After each insertion, output the current median.\n\nThe median is:\n- The middle value if the current count is odd.\n- The average of the two middle values if even; print as X.5 if not a whole number.\n\nThis is a harder version of problem 08: the input stream is larger and contains mixed patterns.",
  "constraints": "1 <= N <= 2*10^4\n-10^6 <= A[i] <= 10^6",
  "inputFormat": "The first line contains N.\nThe second line contains N space-separated integers.",
  "outputFormat": "N lines, one per insertion, each the current median.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": "5\n1 3 5 2 4",
      "output": "1\n2\n3\n2.5\n3",
      "explanation": "After 1:[1]->1. After 3:[1,3]->2. After 5:[1,3,5]->3. After 2:[1,2,3,5]->2.5. After 4:[1,2,3,4,5]->3."
    },
    {
      "input": "6\n6 5 4 3 2 1",
      "output": "6\n5.5\n5\n4.5\n4\n3.5",
      "explanation": "Descending stream; medians decrease."
    }
  ],
  "starterCode": {
